  "limitations": [
    "No physical-device audio, audio-focus/headset, OEM engine, background/lock-screen or battery measurement was performed.",
    "Pitch-snap is experimental chromatic speech sound design, not studio-grade singing autotune or voice cloning.",
    "Offline use requires downloaded Android voice data; Android voices marked online may send text through the Android engine service.",
    "Effects require 16-bit PCM WAV output from the system TTS service. Unsupported formats fail clearly; Neutral uses direct Android speech.",
    "Effects add sentence-level synthesis/processing latency and small reverb/delay tails. Neutral bypasses them.",
    "Native PCM processing has an 8 MiB file limit, a 30-second-per-segment limit, a single worker and a bounded queue.",
    "All dependencies and native sources were not subjected to a full penetration test. No guarantee that every vulnerability or hidden backdoor has been found or eliminated.",
    "Existing API-key/vault storage and OS backup policy are unchanged; a broader at-rest security redesign was not attempted."
  ]
